WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.569
Two weeks had passed since Anne arrived at Green Gables.

2
00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:09.708
She had been very busy, acquainting herself with every tree, shrub, and plant.

3
00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:14.027
After her discoveries Anne would run home and tell Matthew and Marilla.

4
00:00:14.028 --> 00:00:18.261
Matthew listened to it all with a smile of enjoyment on his face.

5
00:00:18.262 --> 00:00:26.210
Marilla listened until she found herself becoming too interested in Anne's adventures, and then she told Anne to be quiet.

6
00:00:26.211 --> 00:00:31.670
Anne was in the orchard one day when the busybody Mrs. Lynde arrived to inspect her.

7
00:00:31.671 --> 00:00:36.875
Mrs. Lynde said to Marilla, "I've heard all about your orphan.

8
00:00:36.876 --> 00:00:41.003
It's too bad there was a mistake. Can't you send her back?"

9
00:00:41.004 --> 00:00:43.934
"We could, but we decided not to.

10
00:00:43.935 --> 00:00:49.832
Matthew liked her, and I must say, I like her too, though she's not perfect.

11
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:54.986
The house is a different place already. She's a bright little thing."

12
00:00:54.987 --> 00:01:01.506
"You have no experience with children, Marilla," Mrs. Lynde said, "and you can't guess how she'll be.

13
00:01:01.507 --> 00:01:04.564
I just hope the situation will be all right."

14
00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:08.621
"I'm not discouraged," was Marilla's dry response.

15
00:01:08.622 --> 00:01:12.974
"I suppose you'd like to see Anne. I'll call her."

16
00:01:12.975 --> 00:01:16.953
Anne ran in with her face flushed from her adventures in the orchard.

17
00:01:16.954 --> 00:01:23.932
But the presence of a stranger was unexpected, and Anne was suddenly shy. She stood near the door.

18
00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:27.306
Anne certainly was an odd-looking girl.

19
00:01:27.307 --> 00:01:33.392
She wore the old, ill-fitting dress from the orphanage, and her hair was messy from running around.

20
00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:38.367
"They didn't choose you for your looks, that's for sure!" began Mrs. Lynde.

21
00:01:38.368 --> 00:01:43.546
"She's very skinny and plain, Marilla. Come here, child, and let me look at you.

22
00:01:43.547 --> 00:01:51.005
How many freckles does she have? And hair as red as carrots! Come closer, child."

23
00:01:51.006 --> 00:01:56.421
Anne came closer but not exactly in the manner that Mrs. Lynde expected.

24
00:01:56.422 --> 00:02:00.283
With one jump Anne stood in front of Mrs. Lynde.

25
00:02:00.284 --> 00:02:05.048
Anne's face was red with anger, and she trembled from head to toe.

26
00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:09.883
"I hate you," she said angrily, stamping her foot on the floor.

27
00:02:09.884 --> 00:02:13.138
"I hate you, I hate you, I hate you!"

28
00:02:13.139 --> 00:02:16.576
She stamped louder each time she spoke.

29
00:02:16.577 --> 00:02:19.874
"How dare you call me ugly and skinny?

30
00:02:19.875 --> 00:02:26.979
How dare you say I have freckles and red hair? You are a rude, unfeeling woman!"

31
00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.499
"Anne!" Marilla gasped.

32
00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:36.011
But Anne was not daunted and continued to face Mrs. Lynde with her head up and her eyes furious.

33
00:02:36.012 --> 00:02:41.652
"How dare you say such things about me?" she cried in a choked voice.

34
00:02:41.653 --> 00:02:47.759
"How would you like to be told you are fat and clumsy and probably don't have any imagination?

35
00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:55.625
I hope I hurt your feelings. I will never forgive you, never, never!" Stamp, stamp

36
00:02:55.626 --> 00:03:01.462
! "Did you ever see such a terrible temper!" exclaimed the horrified Mrs.

37
00:03:01.463 --> 00:03:11.939
Lynde. "Anne, go to your room and stay there until I come up!" Marilla said, recovering her powers of speech with some

38
00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:18.363
difficulty. Anne burst into tears, ran through the hall, up the stairs, and slammed the bedroom

39
00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:22.007
door. "Well, good luck with her," said Mrs.

40
00:03:22.008 --> 00:03:26.526
Lynde. "You shouldn't have said those things about her, Rachel," Marilla

41
00:03:26.527 --> 00:03:31.563
said. "What?" said Mrs. Lynde. "Whose side are you on,

42
00:03:31.564 --> 00:03:36.106
Marilla?" "I'm not trying to excuse her," said Marilla

43
00:03:36.107 --> 00:03:41.953
slowly. "She was very naughty. But nobody has taught Anne what is

44
00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:45.116
right. And you did say too much,

45
00:03:45.117 --> 00:03:49.195
Rachel." "I will be very careful when I visit again,

46
00:03:49.196 --> 00:03:57.169
Marilla. An orphan is more important than I am, that's clear!" said Mrs. Lynde and walked out the door in a huff.

47
00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:04.499
Marilla went upstairs, where she found Anne face-down on the bed, crying. "Anne," said Marilla.

48
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:08.735
There was no answer. "Anne," Marilla said louder.

49
00:04:08.736 --> 00:04:10.856
"Get off the bed and listen now!"

50
00:04:10.857 --> 00:04:13.183
Anne sat up and looked at the floor.

51
00:04:13.184 --> 00:04:19.171
"Mrs. Lynde will certainly have a nice story about you to tell everyone," Marilla went on.

52
00:04:19.172 --> 00:04:25.148
"You must go and say sorry to Mrs. Lynde. You must ask her to forgive you."

53
00:04:25.149 --> 00:04:30.683
"I can never say sorry," said Anne. "You can punish me, Marilla.

54
00:04:30.684 --> 00:04:39.022
You can put me in a deep, dark dungeon with snakes and feed me bread and water. I will not say sorry."

55
00:04:39.023 --> 00:04:46.957
"There aren't any dungeons in Avonlea. But you will stay in your room until you say sorry to Mrs. Lynde."

56
00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:50.790
"Then I will stay here forever," Anne replied.

57
00:04:50.791 --> 00:04:55.115
"I am not sorry. I am happy I said those things!"

58
00:04:55.116 --> 00:05:06.043
At that, Marilla left the room. Downstairs, Marilla told Matthew the story, impressing upon him the seriousness of Anne's misbehavior.

59
00:05:06.044 --> 00:05:10.038
"Mrs. Lynde is an old gossip!" Matthew retorted.

60
00:05:10.039 --> 00:05:17.591
"Matthew! I'm astonished! Don't you think Anne should be punished?" Marilla asked.

61
00:05:17.592 --> 00:05:22.026
"Yes, of course," Matthew answered. "But not too much.

62
00:05:22.027 --> 00:05:25.204
You will give her something to eat while she stays in her room?"

63
00:05:25.205 --> 00:05:33.022
"When do I starve people, Matthew?" said Marilla angrily. "Matthew was no help," she thought.

64
00:05:33.023 --> 00:05:37.079
Marilla brought breakfast, lunch, and dinner to Anne's bedroom.

65
00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.482
Anne still did not want to say sorry.

66
00:05:40.483 --> 00:05:46.666
Matthew crept upstairs and went to her room. "Anne," he whispered, "how are you?"

67
00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:49.755
"I'm all right. It is lonely, though."

68
00:05:49.756 --> 00:05:55.178
Anne smiled sadly, thinking of the many years she would stay in the room.

69
00:05:55.179 --> 00:05:59.804
"Anne, how about you say sorry soon?" Matthew whispered again.

70
00:05:59.805 --> 00:06:05.649
"Well, I am sorry now," Anne admitted. "But I can't tell Mrs. Lynde.

71
00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:12.496
It would be so humiliating. But I will do anything for you, if you really want me to."

72
00:06:12.497 --> 00:06:17.148
"Of course I want you to say sorry. It's too quiet without you, Anne.

73
00:06:17.149 --> 00:06:20.322
Just go and say sorry, there's a good girl."

74
00:06:20.323 --> 00:06:22.633
"Very well," said Anne.

75
00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:25.369
"But don't tell Marilla I asked you."

76
00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:30.772
"I won't," said Anne. Matthew left, surprised by his success.

77
00:06:30.773 --> 00:06:36.793
Then Anne leaned over the stair banisters. "Marilla, I'm ready to say sorry."

78
00:06:36.794 --> 00:06:39.714
Anne and Marilla went to Mrs. Lynde's house.

79
00:06:39.715 --> 00:06:45.372
As they walked, Anne did not look sorry. In fact, she looked very happy.

80
00:06:45.373 --> 00:06:48.776
"What are you thinking, Anne?" Marilla asked.

81
00:06:48.777 --> 00:06:52.788
"I'm thinking of what to say to Mrs. Lynde," Anne said.

82
00:06:52.789 --> 00:06:56.277
Marilla was suspicious but said nothing.

83
00:06:56.278 --> 00:07:02.781
As usual, Mrs. Lynde sat at the kitchen window, watching everything that went on outside the house.

84
00:07:02.782 --> 00:07:07.604
Anne suddenly kneeled in front of the surprised Mrs. Lynde and spoke.

85
00:07:07.605 --> 00:07:12.016
"Oh, Mrs. Lynde, I am so, so sorry.

86
00:07:12.017 --> 00:07:16.908
There are not enough words in the dictionary to say how sorry I am.

87
00:07:16.909 --> 00:07:23.099
What you said was true: my hair is red, and I'm freckled and skinny and ugly.

88
00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:30.186
What I said was true too, but I shouldn't have said it. Please, please, please forgive me."

89
00:07:30.187 --> 00:07:33.018
There was no doubt Anne was sincere.

90
00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:38.655
But unlike Marilla, Mrs. Lynde did not realize that Anne was also having fun.

91
00:07:38.656 --> 00:07:42.480
It was very dramatic, and Anne loved drama.

92
00:07:42.481 --> 00:07:48.080
Mrs. Lynde just said, "Get up, child. Of course I forgive you.

93
00:07:48.081 --> 00:07:53.472
Your hair is a terrible color, but maybe it will change when you grow up."

94
00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:58.805
"Oh, thank you, Mrs. Lynde," Anne said. "You give me hope!"

95
00:07:58.806 --> 00:08:10.199
With that, Mrs. Lynde was satisfied.

